>Side question for foocubi meetings : when all stats are maxed except 
>charisma, what would you suggest for raising CHA ? Quaffing !GA seems 
>just a waste... they could be so useful for alchemy. 

  Potions of Gain Ability have no use in alchemy, except for random
chance.  Gain Energy and Gain Level are the useful ones.

  Other methods of raising charisma are rings of adornment and wearing a
cornuthaum as a wizard, and of course magic traps.

>Is using a magic trap better? 

  I love them.  In addition to the possible charisma gain, when the
magic trap explodes you will also gain some max Pw.

>And what precautions should be taken ?

  Two things: monsters will be generated around you, and 

  - occasionally you'll get burnt.  
    - If you don't have fire resistance you will lose max Hp.  
      - So have fire resistance.
        - ring of fire resistance.
        - intrinsic.
    - Any external armor can be burnt.  
    - Wear expendable armor or armor that resists fire damage.  
  - You'll be blinded every time you activate the trap.
    - Wear gloves in the event of a cockatrice corpse.
      - Feeling around while blind without gloves and touching a 
        cockatrice corpse is an instant death.
    - Better yet, wear a blindfold or a towel.
      - The resulting blindness prevents external blinding.
      - Just remove it to unblind yourself.
  - As a wizard, wield Magicbane for Magic Resistance.  
    - Then you don't have to risk the Cloak of Magic Resistance.
      - If the Cloak of MR is already burnt, it can't be hurt by further
        burning.
  - Be prepared for mind flayers to be generated.
    - Have ESP or telepathy so you can sense them while blind.
    - wand or spell of teleport away in emergency.
    - Grease your helm.
    - You'll be blind so engraving Elbereth is unlikely to succeed
      - even with Magicbane.
    - Use the blindfold trick to make unblinding easy.

  - Have some pets to help deal with the monsters.
    - When you gain charisma you'll automatically tame any monsters 
      around you.

