  Neither.  A fully developed wizard is just hampered in spell casting
by Gauntlets of Power.  A human wizard at Str:18/** has all the
advantages of Gauntlets of Power.  An elven wizard can be an even better
spell caster than a human wizard.  

  XL:30 spell casting by a wizard beats Gauntlets of Power all hollow.
GoP add +6 damage per hit.  XL:30 spell of magic missile averages 56
points of damage per hit per monster.

  (Even at XL:30 a wizard wearing a small shield and Gauntlets of Power
will have non-zero failure rates on some spells.  I don't like that.  I
do like wearing a small shield for 6 more points of AC.  "If more is
better, too much is just right.")

>
>Or maybe you were talking about regular non magical leather gloves... 
>but in this case why not use GoD if you have them ? Sure they don't do 
>much but at least they don't hinder spellcasting. Just curious to have 
>your opinion.

  No problem.  One big reason to use regular gloves: all the gloves
you'll find from the dead soldiers at Fort Ludios and the Castle.
You're almost certain to find at least +3 enchantment, probably better.
That saves more scrolls of Enchant Armor.  

  When you find them you can use confused cursed scroll of Destroy Armor
to fireproof them.  That saves even more scrolls of Enchant Armor.
(That trick actually works with all armor.)  Scrolls of Destroy Armor
take less marker charges to write than scrolls of Enchant Armor.  That
saves marker charges for yet more scrolls of Enchant Armor.  

  I *like* scrolls of Enchant Armor, but only for enchanting armor *up*.
Confused cursed ?oDestroyArmor, found enchantments, and spell of Drain
Life can take the place of a lot of scrolls of Enchant armor.


  I've found +5 gloves and +5 small shield before (although not in the
same game).  Just fireproof them with confused cursed scroll of Destroy
Armor and they're good to go.



